/*
:name: loop_runtime_break
:type: equiv
:verilog_top: loop_runtime_break.top
:pyrope_top: top
*/
// A `break` whose condition is only known at RUNTIME is LEGAL Pyrope: the loop
// bound is still comptime, so the hardware is the priority structure the golden
// spells out — iteration `i` contributes iff no earlier iteration's condition
// held. Same shape as `if cond { <mod call> }`, which is what the conditional
// replicated Sub (todo_loop_cond_sub.md rule 13, the per-replica `next_active`
// chain) exists to express.
//
// It is NOT implemented yet on either path: the default unroll path refuses it
// (`loop-runtime-break`, added because walking the unknown-condition arm used
// to abandon the rest of iteration 0 and every later one, silently compiling
// this to `total = 0`), and the roller declines any body holding loop control.
// This fixture states the CORRECT answer, so it fails until one of them can
// produce it — a refusal is progress over the old miscompile, not the goal.
//
// A COMPTIME break (`if i == 5 { break }`) already works — see
// tests/sim/loop_cond_break_no_sub.prp.

pub mod top(stop:u8) -> (total:u12@[0]) {
  mut acc:u12 = 0
  for i in 0..<8 {
    if stop#[i] { break }
    acc = acc + 1
  }
  total = acc
}
